<!--
  Reference-only. Fetched live from GitHub (the GitHub API is reachable from
  this environment) while implementing TriasDepartureProviderTest, from
  https://github.com/VDVde/TRIAS/issues/1 - the plan doc
  (docs/departures-widget-plan.md, "Data source: TRIAS API via MobiData BW")
  describes this issue as containing "a real example StopEventRequest/
  response". That description does not hold up: the issue is titled
  "Example request to trias service" and its body/comments only demonstrate
  a LocationInformationRequest (looking up a stop by name, "Düsseldorf"),
  never a StopEventRequest or StopEventResponse. No StopEventRequest/
  StopEventResponse example exists in that issue to fetch.

  Kept here, unused by any test, purely as provenance for that finding (and
  because it's still a genuine, real, confirmed-working example TRIAS
  envelope, useful as a reference for the outer Trias/ServiceRequest/
  siri:RequestTimestamp shape used by TriasDepartureProvider.
  buildStopEventRequest()). TriasDepartureProviderTest's actual
  StopEventResponse fixture (trias-stop-event-response.xml, in this same
  directory) is instead hand-built from the official Trias_StopEvents.xsd
  schema, also fetched live from github.com/VDVde/TRIAS - see that fixture's
  own header comment.

  The body below is the working example posted by GitHub user "forgemo" in
  a comment on that issue (quoted verbatim, reformatted only for indentation
  consistency with this file's own style):

  URL: the endpoint you have access to
  METHOD: POST
  HEADERS: Content-Type: text/xml
-->
<Trias version="1.2" xmlns="http://www.vdv.de/trias" xmlns:siri="http://www.siri.org.uk/siri">
    <ServiceRequest>
        <siri:RequestTimestamp>2019-02-17T12:14:01.139+01:00</siri:RequestTimestamp>
        <RequestPayload>
            <LocationInformationRequest>
                <InitialInput>
                    <LocationName>Düsseldorf</LocationName>
                </InitialInput>
            </LocationInformationRequest>
        </RequestPayload>
    </ServiceRequest>
</Trias>
